          "Lead with housing affordability and homeownership access for a constituency with a 33.5% renter rate and a $65,135 median income — this is the material economic concern that will determine whether Hispanic voters view the incumbent as delivering on their economic mobility goals or as taking their support for granted.",
          "Engage the renter constituency specifically on housing costs, tenant protections, and the relationship between housing stability and economic opportunity — renters at 33.5% are a meaningful plurality and a swing constituency in a district where Hispanic voters include both renters navigating affordability and homeowners managing property costs.",
          "Build relationships with Hispanic business owners and small employers on regulatory burden, tax clarity, and economic development — a 40% college-attainment district with middle-class income signals entrepreneurial capacity, and messaging that demonstrates respect for economic self-determination is the pathway to Hispanic voter consolidation that goes beyond demographic assumption."
