          "Sustain Hispanic voter engagement through community presence and specific constituent service, not assumed loyalty; at 59.27%, the Hispanic majority is large enough to hold the seat, but small enough that declining turnout or candidate preference shifts among younger Hispanic adults can meaningfully narrow the margin.",
          "Monitor the college-attainment rate and workforce pipeline carefully; at 30.1%, NM-HD-16's college completion is below state average, and the pathway from secondary education to middle-class employment is the fundamental economic opportunity question that shapes younger adults' evaluation of whether government is delivering for them."
