          "Engage the college-educated professional constituency (41.9%) with specificity on education funding, public school quality, and economic opportunity for knowledge workers; this group is large enough to be decisive and swing-capable based on whether they believe government is delivering on their material interests.",
          "Recognize that 44.8% Hispanic population does not equal monolithic Latino voting bloc: Hispanic professionals, small business owners, and renters have different economic interests and policy priorities; messaging that treats all Hispanic voters as a single constituency misses the real swing dynamics in this district.",
          "Consolidate younger adult voters (37.5 median age) around specific governance outcomes on healthcare access, job creation, and climate/environmental quality rather than abstract partisan positioning; in a 54-46 district, turnout and persuasion among 18-45-year-olds is the margin of victory."
