          { name: "Assuming that Democratic Registration = Durable Voter Mobilization", tag: "avoid", why: "NM-HD-21's demographic alignment with Democratic interests does not automatically produce turnout or sustained loyalty in a constituency where economic conditions are precarious and constituent expectations are high. Renters at $54,611 income are responsive to whether their representative is solving their problems, not to partisan identity. A future challenger running on tenant rights, wage growth, or specific neighborhood service failures could activate this constituency if the incumbent is perceived as taking it for granted. Democratic electoral security in this district depends on active constituent delivery, not on demographic determinism." }
