          "Build an explicit coalition strategy between Hispanic (32.33%) and white (55.08%) voters on cost-of-living specifics: housing affordability, healthcare costs, and childcare access are shared economic concerns across demographic lines that a candidate can use to build durable support beyond the current 54% margin.",
          "Engage the 5.11% Asian community with institutional specificity rather than token recognition: northern New Mexico's Asian population likely includes healthcare professionals, technology workers, and small business owners whose economic integration into professional sectors creates specific policy concerns around professional licensing, business regulation, and workplace equity — these are not generic 'Asian' issues, they are economic concerns with policy solutions.",
