          "Defend and mobilize the Hispanic voter base through specific messaging on housing affordability, healthcare access (particularly for working families), and education quality—the 28.4% and growing Hispanic constituency is persuadable on economics and not reliably Democratic; turnout and candidate preference cannot be assumed.",
          "Address white homeowner economic concerns directly: property tax fairness, school quality, and neighborhood safety are not Republican issues—they are material issues for a 59% white, 80% homeowner-profile constituency that the current 56-44 margin indicates is split and evaluating on performance, not identity.",
