          { name: "Assuming Low College Attainment Means Low Civic Engagement or Organizing Capacity", tag: "avoid", why: "At 24.2% college attainment—the lowest in the data—this is a working-class constituency, not an unsophisticated one. Working-class communities have deep experience with labor organizing, community mutual aid, and collective action around material concerns like wages, housing, and healthcare. Any candidate who assumes low college attainment means low organizing capacity or civic sophistication misunderstands the potential mobilization capacity of a young, Hispanic, working-class district where these communities have demonstrated strong organizational infrastructure when motivated around economic and family stability concerns." }
