          "Invest explicitly in the ~6.4% American Indian/Alaska Native population concentrated in northern reaches of the district: tribal sovereignty, Indian Health Service access, and the state-tribal relationship in the Taos and Pueblo communities are governance obligations that require specific legislative attention and partnership, not generic minority outreach.",
          "Address the college-attainment gap directly: at 24.4%, this district's workforce relies on technical trades and vocational training, not four-year degrees — workforce development policy, apprenticeship access, and occupational licensing that doesn't artificially restrict opportunity are the education issues that actually matter here.",
