          { name: "Generic Minority Coalition Framing Without Specific Constituent Attention", tag: "avoid", why: "NM-56 contains both a 27.96% Hispanic population and a 14.8% Native American gap, and conflating these communities into undifferentiated 'Democratic coalition' or 'minority vote' messaging obscures the distinct economic concerns of each group and risks losing both to a challenger who addresses their specific needs with greater credibility. Hispanic families face particular economic pressures around wages and education access; Native American constituents have governance and sovereignty concerns; and aging homeowners have property tax and healthcare concerns — lumping these together into generic coalition language leaves all three constituencies underserved and vulnerable to a more attentive opponent." }
