          "Avoid treating the 57% as a durable majority; in a district with equal Hispanic and white populations, no dominant age or education profile, and a near-median income level, the current margin depends on candidate performance and constituent satisfaction, not structural Republican advantage — any challenger with credible positioning on local issues and community mobilization capacity can make this seat genuinely competitive."
