          "Engage young adults' wage and economic mobility concerns: the 30.2-year median age and 7.3% college attainment signal a workforce economy where most residents are not college-educated and depend on wage-level jobs. Advocate for wage standards, skills training access, apprenticeship partnerships, and local employer development that creates pathways to economic security without requiring a four-year degree.",
          "Serve the Latino community with specificity on healthcare access and family economic security: while 75% Hispanic makes this a Latino-majority district, most legislative engagement remains generic. Bilingual constituent services, targeted outreach on Medicaid and ACA enrollment, workplace healthcare access, and family economic security programs should be explicit components of constituent service and legislative messaging.",
          "Do not treat an unopposed cycle as evidence of seat safety: unopposed outcomes in heavily partisan districts often mask underlying economic dissatisfaction or low turnout among core constituencies. Use the 2024 cycle to build constituent relationships and demonstrate concrete delivery on working-class economic concerns — not to coast on a Democratic registration advantage that can shift if voters conclude the incumbent is not delivering."
