          "Consolidate the renter and younger-adult constituency (the 21.8% renter rate and 36.1 median age signal a non-trivial share of economic-security-conscious voters) with specific attention to housing costs, student debt, and wage trajectory—these voters are not yet locked into either party and will move toward whoever credibly demonstrates investment in their economic future.",
          "Treat 52% as a plurality, not a majority—the 48% Republican opposition in a Hispanic-plurality, college-educated, middle-income district is not a floor but an active threat; any incumbent or challenger who campaigns as though they have won the district's trust without continuing to earn it through specific economic delivery will find that margin collapse in a competitive environment.",
