          { name: "Assuming Hispanic & Minority Communities Are Safely Republican", tag: "avoid", why: "With 28.48% Hispanic population and an ~6.7% American Indian gap in a high-income, educated district, assuming these communities are reliably Republican without specific engagement on their economic and political concerns is a missed opportunity and potential vulnerability. Hispanic homeowners and business owners in affluent New Mexico communities often have distinct perspectives on immigration policy, labor issues, and community investment that require direct candidate engagement rather than assumption of loyalty. Treating these communities as subgroups of the homeowner majority rather than as constituencies with their own political agency is both strategically weak and substantively incomplete." }
