          "Lead with housing affordability and economic opportunity for renters and younger professionals: in a $118K-income district with 22% renters, the gap between nominal income and actual housing costs is driving dissatisfaction; specific proposals on renter protections, housing development, and workforce development are more credible than abstract tax policy.",
          "Engage the 26% Hispanic/Latino and 10% Asian constituencies with specificity on education quality, healthcare access, and economic mobility pathways — communities this educated and this economically integrated evaluate on whether government delivers tangible outcomes for their families, not partisan tribal identity.",
          "Consolidate homeowner and business confidence through demonstrated competence on property tax fairness, education funding, and infrastructure — but recognize that this 53% margin is not stable unless the candidate simultaneously addresses renter and minority-community economic concerns; a 53% result in a 60%-college-educated district is a warning, not a floor."
