          "Engage the 20.5% renter constituency with specific policy: renters are one in five households in NM-SD-23 and represent a population segment without homeowner-stability anchors; housing affordability, tenant protections, and cost-of-living advocacy are concrete ways to consolidate this swing constituency rather than assuming it defaults to Democratic voting.",
          "Account for the ~8.5% demographic gap: the gap between reported Census categories and 100% likely represents American Indian/Alaska Native residents whose civic participation and policy priorities may not align with the partisan baseline; authentic engagement with tribal governments and Native American constituents is both a governance obligation and a defense against losing these voters to low turnout or an alternative.",
          "Lead with material outcomes on the issues college-educated voters evaluate: education quality metrics, healthcare access and cost, housing affordability progress, and workforce development are the specific policy domains where Pope's record will be measured; generic partisan messaging is less persuasive to a 39.6% college-educated constituency than demonstrable evidence of concrete delivery."
