          "Lead with economic security messaging grounded in the $42,663 median income and 29.5% renter rate: housing affordability, healthcare costs, and wage stability are the material concerns of this district's working-class base—both the Anglo homeowner plurality and the Hispanic renter-and-working-class majority. Candidates who communicate specifically on these issues gain traction regardless of partisan framing.",
          "Engage the Hispanic working-class and renter constituency with cultural fluency and specific economic policy: the 58% Hispanic composition means that winning—or holding—this seat requires genuine engagement of Spanish-speaking families' economic concerns, not token outreach. Bilingual presence, community organization, and Spanish-language economic messaging are competitive necessities, not optional enhancements.",
