          { name: "Partisan Ideology Positioning Over Material Economic Concern", tag: "avoid", why: "NM-SD-35's demographic profile — nearly half Hispanic/Latino, median income $56,364, 43.9-year median age, significant renter population — is not naturally organized around abstract partisan ideological divides but around concrete economic security concerns: housing affordability, wage stagnation, healthcare access, and property tax management. A legislator who defaults to generic partisan rhetoric about government size or regulatory burden rather than specific answers to these material concerns misses the opportunity to anchor their political position in the lived economic reality of most constituents. In a district this economically diverse and ethnically plural, material economic governance matters more than ideological positioning — and credibility flows from specific policy answers to concrete problems." }
