          "Engage the 53% Hispanic community with specific economic development and workforce priorities rather than symbolic inclusion: Hispanic voter participation and preference in SD-37 are conditional on whether state policy is reducing barriers to small-business access, workforce training, and housing stability—areas where legislative action directly affects Hispanic household economic security.",
          "Treat an unopposed 2024 result as a baseline, not a ceiling: the combination of younger voters, renters, and college-educated constituents are precisely the groups most likely to mobilize against an incumbent perceived as not delivering on housing, education, or healthcare—and the absence of a 2024 challenger does not protect against a credible future challenger if constituent engagement and legislative delivery lapse."
