          "Engage the Hispanic-majority constituency (57.6%) and the ~4.5% AIAN gap population with equal institutional attention; northern New Mexico's economic and cultural identity is rooted in both communities, and governing without genuine partnership with both is leaving constituency needs unmet.",
          "Address the college-attainment gap (29.6%) and the renter population's economic vulnerability (16.3%): higher education access, workforce training pipelines, and housing affordability are the material issues that determine whether young adults and working families can build economic mobility in the district.",
          "Build constituent service infrastructure that creates direct relationships rather than relying on partisan loyalty; the unopposed result masks whether constituents actually know their legislator or whether they simply have no alternative — that distinction becomes electorally urgent the moment opposition appears."
